{"sections":[{"type":"Meta","title":"Hartlepool's employment, unemployment and economic inactivity - ONS","description":"How Hartlepool (E06000001) compares with the North East and Great Britain across employment-related statistics","contentTitle":"Labour market robo reports","releaseDate":"20240514","lastUpdated":"2024-05-14","outputSeries":"labourmarketindicatorsbyunitaryandlocalauthoritiesgreatbritain","contentType":"robo-journalism"},{"type":"Header","title":"Employment, unemployment and economic inactivity in Hartlepool","standfirst":"How Hartlepool compares with the North East and Great Britain across employment-related statistics","label":"Select a different local authority"},{"type":"Notice","content":"<p>This pilot publication is no longer being updated. Feedback to help us develop future publications can be sent to our <a href = \"mailto: subnational@ons.gov.uk\">subnational analysis team</a>.</p>"},{"id":"section-top","type":"Summary","title":"In Hartlepool:","content":"<a name=\"section-top\"></a>","sections":[{"indicator":"Employment rate","value":"67.9%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Employment in Hartlepool has decreased slightly compared with the previous year. Hartlepool's employment rate was lower than across the North East as a whole in the year ending December 2023.</p><p><a href=\"#employment-rate\">Go to employment rate section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Unemployment rate","value":"4.3%","note":"ages 16+","content":"<p>Unemployment (people looking for work) has fallen since a year earlier. The unemployment rate for Hartlepool was higher than across the North East as a whole.</p><p><a href=\"#unemployment\">Go to unemployment rate section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Claimant Count","value":"5.1%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Claimant Count was lower in March 2024 compared with a year earlier. The <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/aguidetolabourmarketstatistics#claimant-count\" rel=\"external\">Claimant Count</a>  measures the number of people who are claiming unemployment-related benefits.         </p><p><a href=\"#claimant-count\">Go to Claimant Count section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Economic inactivity","value":"29.7%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Economic inactivity has increased since the previous year. These are people who are neither employed nor seeking work.</p><p><a href=\"#inactivity\">Go to economic inactivity section</a>  &darr;</p>"}]},{"id":"caveat","type":"Warning","content":"<p> These estimates are less precise than national or regional figures because they are based on smaller numbers of survey respondents.</p><p> Local population changes also mean that the numbers of people in each area who are employed, unemployed and economically inactive in this article may be under- or over-estimates.</p>"},{"type":"survey","content":"<p>Estimates of employment and economic inactivity are based on the <a href= \"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/annualpopulationsurveyapsqmi\" rel=\"external\">Annual Population Survey</a>. Unemployment estimates are modelled to improve their precision compared to those based only on responses provided via the Annual Population Survey.</p><p>The Claimant Count is based on administrative data from the benefits system. These data are experimental statistics.</p>"},{"id":"employment-rate","title":"Employment in Hartlepool has decreased slightly compared with the previous year","content":"<p>Hartlepool's employment rate was lower than across the North East as a whole in the year ending December 2023.</p><p>Of people aged 16 to 64 years living in Hartlepool, 67.9% were employed in the year ending December 2023. This is a slight decrease compared with the year ending December 2022 when the local rate was 68.2%.</p><p>Across the North East in the year ending December 2023, 72.8% of people aged 16 to 64 years were employed. This was higher compared with the previous year, when 70.5% of people were employed.</p>"},{"id":"chart-timeseries","type":"Chart","chartType":"line-highlight","title":"Employment rates of areas in the North East","subtitle":"Among those aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending December 2013 to year ending December 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2013","y":59.1},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2014","y":64.7},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2015","y":65.1},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2016","y":67.8},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2017","y":66.7},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2018","y":68.4},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2019","y":67.2},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2020","y":71.3},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2021","y":69.7},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2022","y":67.7},{"z":"Newcastle upon Tyne","x":"2023","y":74.3},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2013","y":73.9},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2014","y":72.8},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2015","y":74},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2016","y":72.1},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2017","y":73},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2018","y":71.8},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2019","y":72.3},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2020","y":71.8},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2021","y":69.8},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2022","y":70.5},{"z":"Northumberland","x":"2023","y":70.8},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2013","y":65.7},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2014","y":68.6},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2015","y":67.3},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2016","y":70.9},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2017","y":71.3},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2018","y":74.6},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2019","y":71.2},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2020","y":71.3},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2021","y":71.1},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2022","y":72.2},{"z":"County Durham","x":"2023","y":74.5},{"z":"Darlington","x":"2013","y":72.9},{"z":"Darlington","x":"2014","y":71.9},{"z":"Darlington","x"